.TH BFSC 1
.SH NAME
bfsc \- BFS (Brainf Script) to Brainfuck compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bfsc
.RI [ options ]
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bfsc
compiles BFS (Brainf Script) source files to Brainfuck.
BFS is a typed domain-specific language with variables, arrays, arithmetic, comparisons,
and control flow that lowers to plain Brainfuck text.
.PP
By default,
.B bfsc
writes the generated Brainfuck to standard output (or to a file with
.BR \-o ).
With
.BR \-c / \-\-compile ,
it continues through the
.B AmazingBF
backend to produce a native x86_64 executable directly.
.PP
If
.I FILE
is
.BR \- ,
source is read from standard input.
.SS Supported types
.TS
l l l.
Type	Cells	Representation
\fBu8\fR	1	wrapping mod 256
\fBu16\fR	2	little-endian (lo byte first)
\fBu32\fR	4	little-endian (lo byte first)
.TE
.SS Language features
Variable declarations, fixed-size arrays, \fBwhile\fR, \fBif\fR/\fBelse\fR,
arithmetic (\fB+ \- * / %\fR), comparisons (\fB< > <= >= == !=\fR),
boolean operators (\fB&& ||\fR), \fBscan()\fR, \fBprint()\fR, \fBputchar()\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Output path.
Without
.BR \-c :
write BF text to
.I PATH
instead of standard output.
With
.BR \-c :
write the compiled executable to
.IR PATH .
Default executable names are
.B a.out
(Linux) and
.B a.exe
(Windows).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compile
Compile the BFS source all the way to a native x86_64 executable via the
.B AmazingBF
backend.
Without this flag,
.B bfsc
only outputs Brainfuck text.
.TP
.BR \-\-target " " \fIx86_64\-linux|x86_64\-windows\fR
Native compilation target (only meaningful with
.BR \-c ).
Linux targets emit ELF executables; Windows targets emit PE32+ console executables.
The default follows the build target of
.BR bfsc .
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-opt\-level " " \fI0|1|2|3\fR
Optimization level passed to the
.B AmazingBF
backend (only meaningful with
.BR \-c ,
default
.BR 3 ).
See
.BR amazingbf (1)
for a description of each level.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress backend progress messages to stderr (only meaningful with
.BR \-c ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Compile .bfs to BF text on stdout
bfsc tests/utils/sort.bfs

# Save BF text to a file, then run it
bfsc tests/utils/sort.bfs \-o /tmp/sort.bf
echo "3 2 1" | AmazingBF /tmp/sort.bf \-q

# Compile .bfs directly to a native Linux executable
bfsc tests/utils/sort.bfs \-c \-o sort

# Compile for Windows (cross-compile)
bfsc tests/utils/sort.bfs \-c \-\-target x86_64\-windows \-o sort.exe

# Pipe BF to AmazingBF when the program does not read stdin
bfsc tests/utils/linear_eq.bfs | AmazingBF \- \-q
.fi
.SH NOTES
When the generated Brainfuck program reads from standard input (e.g.\& the BFS source
uses
.BR scan() ),
write the BF text to a file first and pass it as a path argument to
.BR AmazingBF .
Piping both the BF code and program input through stdin simultaneously does not work.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amazingbf (1),
.B cargo run \-\-bin bfsc \-\- \-\-help
